 "scale_correction_pct": 6.559,
 "note": "The model is scaled so its wheelbase is exactly the published 3.125 m, so the wheelbase row agrees by construction and every other row is a real test. The tyre-diameter cross-check agrees to within 1%, which is a genuinely independent check because it does not use the axles at all. Two caveats worth stating: the published 1.870 m is the BODY width and width_without_mirrors_m is what is compared, while width_overall_incl_mirrors_m is the full bounding box and is wider; and the model's own proportions are internally inconsistent with the published spec by a few percent, so no single scale factor makes every row exact - anchoring on the wheelbase leaves the length about 2.6% long, while anchoring on the tyre diameter would leave the wheelbase 1% short and the length about 1.6% short. The wheelbase anchor is used because it is the dimension the vehicle is actually specified and measured by."
